<task id="034" project="field-mapping-server-write-path-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Inbound communication and document ingestion stay outside RecordCreationService as named exceptions; guards pin them (FR-21 part b, W3 direction)</title>
    <phase>3 W3 Product creators onto the service</phase>
    <gate>019 complete</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Adds source-scan guards and may touch .cs in Sprk.Bff.Api if a guard reveals a missing owner call (data-mutation, security-adjacent: owner and isolation of inbound rows); adds tests at KEEP paths (TEST-MODIFYING override).</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Re-scoped 2026-11-07 under the W3 direction. The remaining work is a closed-set guard task with a decision rule (fix a missing owner call in scope, or stop and report); a Sonnet agent at high effort executed it from this POML.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>W3-server</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>true</parallel-safe>
    <deps>019</deps>
    <tags>bff-api, communication, documents, ownership, testing, guard</tags>
    <estimated-effort>4-6 hours</estimated-effort>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>RE-SCOPED 2026-11-07 under the W3 direction (notes/decisions.md "W3 direction", 2026-11-06, its "034" bullet; "033 dropped", 2026-11-07). The inbound ingestors do NOT move onto `RecordCreationService`. They stay outside it as named-exception creators, and guards pin each one. A named-exception creator is valid when it calls the same invariant-owner classes (I-1 stamp, record-first owner, mapping engine where it applies, secure gates) for every invariant its table carries, and a guard pins: "this creator writes this table and calls these owners, and no other creator does". The guards pin (1) the dedupe on the message id, (2) the unfiled-communication creator exception on the ingestor path ONLY, and (3) attachment ownership through the same resolver. If a guard reveals an ingestor that does NOT call an owner its table needs, that is a defect: fix it in scope with a test that fails first; if the fix is large or changes behaviour users see, STOP and report instead. The original text (route through the service with the system principal, a new create option, a carried-owner input) is superseded and not to be built. Reference: notes/task-034-notes.md (inventory and the four service gaps that W3 declines to close in R1).</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE platform developer, .NET 10 BFF, inbound email/messaging ingestion and Dataverse ownership. Follow ADRs strictly.</role>
  <goal>Every inbound-ingestion creator is a named exception with a source-scan guard that pins its table, its owner calls and its dedupe; the unfiled-communication creator exception is exercised by the ingestor path only (the unified service refuses it); attachment rows take their owner from the same resolver as their communication; no ingestor gains a new principal; the build, the filtered BFF tests and the ArchTests pass.</goal>

  <context>
    <background>spec.md FR-21 part b (amended by the W3 direction), FR-09, NFR-01. Ownership of an inbound row is already decided by `IRecordOwnershipResolver` (task 146, UAC-r2): `IncomingCommunicationProcessor` and `EmailUploadCaptureService` evaluate the association BEFORE the create (`IncomingAssociationResolver.OwnershipContextForNewRecordAsync`, with the FR-26 core-ancestor stamps derived inside it), ask `ResolveOwnerAsync`, and create the row with the team and the filing fields (`BuildNewRecordFieldsAsync`) or, when unfiled, keep the creator (E1, owner round 10 item 8, 2026-10-03). The attachment documents, attachment rows and the archived .eml carry the communication's resolved owner (`ApplyOwner`), never a second resolution. Dedupe: the two email ingestors create the communication through `CreateCommunicationRaceProofAsync` (UNIQUE alternate key on `sprk_internetmessageid`); `IncomingCommunicationProcessor` also checks the Graph message id and the canonical internet message id first; `MessagingIngestor` is deduped on the ACS message id in `IncomingMessagingJobHandler` (idempotency key, lock, re-check, ingest, mark). `RecordCreationService` refuses an unfiled create on a table with an `OwnershipException` (`record_creation.ownership_exception`), so the exception is honoured only outside the service. Census: `RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests` already lists the email ingestors and the chat-attachment materializer as Routed (the resolver, not the service) and `MessagingIngestor` as a Permanent waiver. UAC-r2 PR #2110 is merged; `CommunicationService.cs` (outbound) is not edited by this task.</background>

    <creator-inventory note="the closed set; line numbers drift, re-grep before use">
      <creator id="C1" file="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Channels/MessagingIngestor.cs" member="PersistAsync" table="sprk_communication" create="IGenericEntityService.CreateAsync">Named exception: an inbound chat message names no record, so the row is created UNFILED and keeps its creator (registry rule `UnfiledCommunicationKeepsCreator`; census Permanent waiver; E1). No owner, no filing, no stamp at create. It is filed only by a record-thread JOIN (`ThreadResolver` -> `IRecordOwnershipResolver.ReparentAsync`). Dedupe: `IncomingMessagingJobHandler` (ACS message id).</creator>
      <creator id="C2" file="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/IncomingCommunicationProcessor.cs" member="CreateCommunicationRecordAsync (decision in ResolveInboundFilingAsync)" table="sprk_communication" create="ICommunicationDataverseService.CreateCommunicationRaceProofAsync">Owner: `IncomingAssociationResolver.EvaluateAsync` -> `OwnershipContextForNewRecordAsync` (I-1 stamps) -> `IRecordOwnershipResolver.ResolveOwnerAsync` -> `BuildNewRecordFieldsAsync` for an owned row; unfiled keeps the creator and `ApplyToNewRecordAsync` writes the association afterwards. A refusal or an undeterminable filing HOLDS the email (`RecordOwnerUnresolvedException`).</creator>
      <creator id="C3" file="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/IncomingCommunicationProcessor.cs" member="ProcessIncomingAttachmentsAsync" table="sprk_document and sprk_communicationattachment" create="IGenericEntityService.CreateAsync (two sites)">Owner CARRIED from C2 through `ApplyOwner(row, owner)`; never re-resolved. Container from `CommunicationContainerResolver` before the upload (I-4).</creator>
      <creator id="C4" file="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/IncomingCommunicationProcessor.cs" member="ArchiveEmlAsync / ArchivedEmlDocument" table="sprk_document" create="IGenericEntityService.CreateAsync">As C3.</creator>
      <creator id="C5" file="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/EmailUploadCaptureService.cs" member="CaptureWithOutcomeAsync" table="sprk_communication" create="ICommunicationDataverseService.CreateCommunicationRaceProofAsync">As C2, with `RequestedBy` = the saving user (`RecordRequester.OfObjectId(userId)`, an authenticated caller, never a message field) and `StampCreatorOn`. A refusal SKIPS the capture.</creator>
      <creator id="C6" file="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Email/EmailAttachmentProcessor.cs" member="ProcessSingleAttachmentAsync" table="sprk_document" create="IDocumentDataverseService.CreateDocumentAsync (a seam that refuses a missing owning team)">`ResolveOwnerAsync(OwnershipOfAttachmentDocument(...))` BEFORE the create; `OwningTeamId` from the answer; a refusal creates nothing. An attachment carries its parent link (`sprk_parentdocument`) and its association in the create, never in the follow-up update (coordinator instruction 2026-11-07, matching task 030b for the Office save): `CreateDocumentRequest.ParentDocumentLookup` and `CreateDocumentRequest.Association` (030b's contract) are staged on the one create entity, and the update writes the file pointer and metadata only. No production caller today (`ProcessAttachmentsAsync` is unused; the sink guard classes it Dead).</creator>
      <creator id="C7" file="src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/MessageAttachmentMaterializer.cs" member="MaterializeAsync" table="sprk_document and sprk_communicationattachment" create="IGenericEntityService.CreateAsync (two sites)">`ResolveOwnerAsync(ContentOf("sprk_communication", id))` BEFORE the upload; `owner.ApplyTo` on both rows; a refusal is a 409 rejection with neither bytes nor rows. Registered, no production caller today.</creator>
      <not-in-scope>Post-persist satellites the ingestors call, each already in the census: `ThreadResolver` and `DirectThreadAccessService` (threads; Direct threads stay a census waiver, E2), `CommunicationParticipantIndexer`, `CommunicationEnrichmentService` (review logs), `CommunicationInternalOnlyFloor`, `DeliveryContextMerge`. The outbound `CommunicationService.cs` (UAC-r2 surface). The Office save of an email (task 030b). `RecordCreationService`, `RecordTableRules` and `OwnedChildWrite` (no change).</not-in-scope>
    </creator-inventory>

    <invariants-by-table note="what each table carries and which class owns it; the guards pin the call, not the class">
      <table name="sprk_communication">I-1 stamp: `CoreAncestorResolver` via `IncomingAssociationResolver` (C2, C5; C1 has no filing at create, a JOIN re-stamps through `ReparentAsync`). I-2 / I-6 owner: `IRecordOwnershipResolver.ResolveOwnerAsync` (C2, C5), the unfiled exception (C1; unfiled C2, C5). Inherited Access Permission: `ResolveInheritedAccessPermissionAsync` inside `ApplyCoreAncestorStampsAsync`. I-3 mapping: no ingestor calls the mapping engine and no seeded profile targets this table for inbound rows; mapping into an inbound row needs the app-only lookup reader the W3 direction keeps out of R1, so it is recorded as an owner question and left to the repair pass (task 052). I-5: the table is not search-indexed.</table>
      <table name="sprk_document (attachment and .eml rows)">I-6 owner: carried (C3, C4) or resolved (C6, C7). I-4 container: `CommunicationContainerResolver` before the upload (C3, C4, C7; C6 takes the caller's drive and has no caller). I-5: no ingestor names the index columns. I-1: a document has no stamp column of its own; its root is read from its typed lookups, so the lookups are written in the create (C6: the parent link and the association; C3, C4: `sprk_relatedcommunication`); its access follows the communication through the child-access reconciler (L4).</table>
      <table name="sprk_communicationattachment">I-6 owner: carried (C3) or resolved (C7). No other invariant.</table>
    </invariants-by-table>

    <relevant-files>
      <file role="new-test">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/InboundIngestionCreatorsGuardTests.cs (creator closed set; owner calls per creator; unfiled exception; attachment ownership; principal; each with must-fire and must-not-fire controls)</file>
      <file role="new-test">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/InboundIngestionDedupeGuardTests.cs (dedupe on the message id for the mailbox, upload and chat paths; each with controls)</file>
      <file role="modify-text-only">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests.cs (the MessagingIngestor waiver reason names the registry rule and the guard; no count or disposition changes)</file>
      <file role="read-only">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Channels/MessagingIngestor.cs</file>
      <file role="read-only">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/IncomingCommunicationProcessor.cs</file>
      <file role="read-only">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/EmailUploadCaptureService.cs</file>
      <file role="read-only">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Email/EmailAttachmentProcessor.cs</file>
      <file role="read-only">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/MessageAttachmentMaterializer.cs</file>
      <file role="read-only">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Jobs/Handlers/IncomingMessagingJobHandler.cs</file>
      <file role="read-only">src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs (CreateCommunicationRaceProofAsync)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/WriterOnlyTablesWritersGuardTests.cs (named creators, source spans, controls)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/CreateOwnerResolutionGuardTests.cs (rule predicate plus Theory controls)</file>
      <file role="canonical-reference">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests.cs (the census this guard sits beside)</file>
    </relevant-files>
    <dependencies>
      <dependency task="019" status="required">W2 service deployed and reviewed (the service's refusal of an unfiled create on an OwnershipException table is part of what is pinned).</dependency>
    </dependencies>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="W3 direction (decisions.md 2026-11-06)">No change to `RecordCreationService`, `RecordTableRules`, `OwnedChildWrite`, or `CommunicationService.cs`. No given-id input, no pinned-owner input, no app-only translator, no new create option. No new production file, registration, endpoint or package.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md section 16 (enforcement ladder)">A guard ships with must-fire and must-not-fire controls. Existing violations, if any, are listed in a ratchet baseline. A mutation of the production source that the guard should catch is run once per rule and recorded in the task notes.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-038">New tests only at KEEP paths (here: `tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/**`; a behaviour test for a fixed gap goes under `tests/integration/data-mutation/**`). No `Mock&lt;HttpMessageHandler&gt;`, no DI-registration tests, no reflection on non-public members. A guard asserts structure of source text; it does not mirror the implementation line by line (assert the owner call and its order, not every statement).</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028 / NFR-01">Inbound external senders are never a principal. `RequestedBy` is set only from an authenticated caller. An unfiled communication keeps the CREATOR (the app identity); no guess of a user or team owner. A filed row whose owner cannot be resolved is refused and writes nothing.</constraint>
    <constraint source="Public repository">Notes, commits and test messages state rules and gaps in neutral terms. Any open access defect goes only in the report to the operator.</constraint>
    <constraint source="CLAUDE.md section 10">If no production .cs under `src/` changes, the BFF placement, publish-size and CVE items are recorded as "no production change"; if one changes, measure per section 10.</constraint>
  </constraints>

  <knowledge>
