    </files>
  </knowledge>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="0" name="Context + rigor declaration">Declare FULL rigor. Re-grep every create of `sprk_communication`, `sprk_communicationattachment` and `sprk_document` and every `CreateCommunicationRaceProofAsync` / `CreateDocumentAsync` call under Services/Communication and Services/Email, and confirm the creator inventory above (C1-C7). A creator not in the inventory is an escalation, not an addition.</step>
    <step order="1">Write the guards (InboundIngestionCreatorsGuardTests, InboundIngestionDedupeGuardTests) with their controls. The rule predicates are static methods over source text so the controls feed them synthetic text.</step>
    <step order="2">For each rule, run one mutation of the production source that the rule must catch (restore it afterwards) and record the failing assertion in notes/task-034-notes.md. If a guard fires on today's source without a mutation, that is a missing owner call: apply the decision rule in the prompt.</step>
    <step order="3">Reword the MessagingIngestor waiver reason in the census to name the registry rule and the guard. No count or disposition changes.</step>
    <step order="4">Build the BFF and ArchTests (0 errors, 0 warnings). Run the filtered BFF tests (`FullyQualifiedName~Communication|FullyQualifiedName~Email|FullyQualifiedName~Ingest|FullyQualifiedName~RecordOwnership`, never unfiltered) and the ArchTests in full.</step>
    <step order="5">Record in notes/task-034-notes.md: the inventory result, the guard list with controls and mutation evidence, the owner questions, and "no production change" (or the fix and its fail-first evidence).</step>
  </steps>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>An ingestor lacks an owner call its table needs and the fix is large or changes behaviour users see: STOP, report the gap and options; do not widen the task.</trigger>
    <trigger>A creator of the three tables exists that is not in the inventory (including a creator reached by a computed table name): STOP and report; do not add an exception without a stated rationale.</trigger>
    <trigger>A guard cannot be written without editing `RecordCreationService`, `RecordTableRules`, `OwnedChildWrite` or `CommunicationService.cs`: STOP; that is an owner-rule change for UAC-r2.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <justification>
    <existing>The census (`RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests`) already counts every create of these tables and requires each Routed file to reach the resolver, and `SecureChildOwnership*` tests pin each writer's owner by behaviour. Nothing pins WHICH creators are ingestors, that the unfiled exception stays on the ingestor path, or the dedupe on the message id.</existing>
    <extension>Yes for the data: the census stays the count authority and gains only a reworded reason. The two guard classes are new test files because the census asserts count and resolver reach per file, not creator-to-table-to-owner-call identity, and the dedupe is a different concern from ownership.</extension>
    <cost-of-doing-nothing>The ingestors sit outside the unified service by owner decision (W3), so only a guard stops a later edit from dropping the race-proof create (duplicate communication rows), re-resolving an attachment's owner, owning an unfiled message by a guess, or adding a new ingestor that skips the owner classes.</cost-of-doing-nothing>
  </justification>

  <tools>
    <tool name="dotnet">Build/test .NET</tool>
  </tools>

  <outputs>
    <output type="test">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/InboundIngestionCreatorsGuardTests.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/InboundIngestionDedupeGuardTests.cs</output>
    <output type="test">tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/RecordOwnerAssignmentCensusTests.cs (reason text only)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/integration/data-mutation/RecordOwnership/EmailAttachmentCreateCarriesLinksTests.cs (AC7 behaviour)</output>
    <output type="test">tests/unit/domain/Dataverse/DocumentParentCreateStagingTests.cs (AC7 stager)</output>
    <output type="code">src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Email/EmailAttachmentProcessor.cs; src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/Models.cs (CreateDocumentRequest.ParentDocumentLookup, [JsonIgnore]); src/server/shared/Spaarke.Dataverse/DataverseServiceClientImpl.cs (StageDocumentParent)</output>
